"Each people has its own account of where it came from. One Bunun account tells of a gourd that fell from the sky and split open, and a man and a woman walked out. The Atayal tell of a great rock that burst apart. The Cou say the god Hamo made them from maple leaves, and that they later moved from Yushan to where they live now. The Kavalan say their ancestors came from islands to the south. Lesson 1 called these words passed down by mouth. They are evidence of another kind: they tell us how a people understands itself, and they deserve the same respect as any other source.": "5d4676d1676e",
